er is asking \"is there any improvement?\" - they want to know if the calibrated retraining actually improved the model compared to the overfitted version. Let me think about what improvements were made and summarize them clearly.\n\nFrom the context, I can compare:\n\n**Before (Overfitted Run):**\n- 60 steps, 5 epochs, loss collapsed to 0.0032\n- r=64, α=128\n- 0 benign samples\n- Model was severely overfitting - memorizing training data\n\n**After (Calibrated Run):**\n- 25 steps, 2 epochs, final loss 0.82\n- r=16, α=32, LR=1e-4, with 108 balanced samples across vuln, benign, and identity categories - much healthier convergence\n\nLooking at test results, identity check passes with correct self-identification, and CWE-89 SQL injection detection correctly flags the vulnerability with proper CVSS scoring. The benign parameterized query test appears to have failed though, showing a false positive.\n\nThere's real progress: healthy loss (0.82 vs the previous 0.003 overfit), correct vulnerability detection still working, identity intact, and training running 4x faster. But the false positive issue on safe parameterized SQL remains unresolved - worth flagging clearly when I present these findings."}
